import LeanUrat.MovesT.TV_B2

/-! # TV-B3 — `mem_cyl_of_child_cyl`: (S-child) ⟹ (S-mem)

BRIDGE CAMPAIGN unit **TV-B3** (area BP3, cluster B; blueprint
`lean/notes/BRIDGE_BP3_TV_2026-07-30.md` §3.B + §4). E-PHASE SKELETON —
statements pinned, bodies `sorry`.

INFORMAL STATEMENT: `TreeModel.mem` is GENERATED by `child` through
`mem_single` (one-node histories) and `mem_snoc` (extensions), so the child
transfer law (S-child) = `StableInputs.child_cyl` implies the mem transfer
(S-mem) at every history, by induction on the history's node list via the
TV-B8 eliminator `History.snoc_induction`.

STATEMENT RESOLUTION (recorded): the unit is stated in TWO layers —
* `tv_b3_mem_transfer_of_child_transfer`, the SINGLE-MODEL CORE at one fixed
  box pair (x, x'): pointwise child transfer at (x, x') gives mem transfer at
  (x, x') for every H. This is the actual induction content (the tower/
  threshold quantifiers play no role in it) and the E5-helper genre the
  blueprint's sketch describes;
* `mem_cyl_of_child_cyl`, the blueprint-named TOWER FORM (S-mem) verbatim:
  from `SI : StableInputs` (TV-B2), at every threshold-passing pair N ≤ N'
  and every level-<n·N-agreeing box pair. Its proof = the core lemma at
  `hchild := fun o ν => SI.child_cyl N hN N' h' hNN' o ν x x' hagree`.

PROOF SKETCH (core lemma): `History.snoc_induction` (TV-B8) on H — singleton
case: `mem_single` rewrites both sides to `child none ν ·`, close by `hchild`;
snoc case: `mem_snoc` rewrites both sides to `mem (some H₀) · ∧ child (some H₀)
ν ·`, close by the IH And-congruent with `hchild`. NOTE: `mem_single`'s carrier
is the raw `⟨[ν], h1.1, h1.2⟩` constructor (MovesD/Defs.lean:638) while TV-B8's
singleton case produces `oneNode ν h` — the prover bridges via the `oneNode`
unfolding (the E5 `mem_oneNode_iff` helper is the in-corpus precedent,
E5_rootSplit.lean:131-193 vicinity).

E-PHASE FINDING carried from TV-B1/TV-B2 (recorded, affects the TOWER form
only): the unguarded tower chart carrier `χat : ∀ N', Fin n → Fin (n * N')` is
uninhabited at n ≥ 1, so `mem_cyl_of_child_cyl` (which binds a `StableInputs`
over such a χat) is vacuously derivable at n ≥ 1 until the Q2/B7 guard repair;
the CORE lemma is χat-free and carries the honest content either way.

deps: B2 (the bundle), B8 (the eliminator, prover-time). Consumed by: TV-B5,
TV-B6. difficulty: hard-fable, ~40 lines. -/

set_option linter.style.longLine false
